        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491290603_872127_95934" xmi:uuid="3c8b8228-2533-4f45-8075-c6330f9478a0" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491337111_946637_130599" xmi:uuid="bde5d85b-78d0-4cec-b2b5-3296eee3d1d9" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491290603_872127_95934"/>
            <body>A PartVersion is an identification of a version of a part. It serves as the collector of the data characterizing a realizable object in various application contexts. &lt;note&gt; A PartVersion is a part that can be produced, consumed, used to produce other PartVersion objects, or offered to the market. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; The collection of defining information can be incomplete, in this case not all of the PartView objects needed to define a PartVersion are associated with the PartVersion. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; The set of all PartVersion objects of a Part represents the history of the Part within a specific life-cycle stage or over its complete life cycle. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; A PartVersion does not have to be referenced by any PartView. &lt;/note&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>PartVersion</name>
          <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491302950_175142_107356" xmi:uuid="13cba0ad-5a37-4522-9f8a-813e73225165" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
