        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491290680_914610_95943" xmi:uuid="3d08b7ef-ef6e-46fc-a0f1-d9d64fd81ba8" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491338491_496681_131312" xmi:uuid="721cae82-b826-4eb1-ac9b-7b3a15cb7dd2" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491290680_914610_95943"/>
            <body>An Occurrence is an occurrence of an object in a product structure that is defined by an item specified by OccurrenceOrOccurrenceDefinitionSelect. &lt;example&gt;In the case of a car, the Item 'wheel' is defined once. Its PartVersion carries all the information necessary to define the wheel (such as its shape) independent of its usage. Additionally, there are 5 Occurrence objects for this wheel since there are 5 equal wheels used in this car: front-left, front-right, rear-left, rear-right, and spare wheel. Each of these instances can carry additional information such as placement or function. Each Occurrence is a DefinitionBasedOccurrence, or a SpecifiedOccurrence. &lt;/example&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>Occurrence</name>
