    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285001_752043_89821" xmi:uuid="2754d9f8-ce3b-4fc9-9329-4cd654e41552" xmi:type="uml:Package">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285089_508143_89899" xmi:uuid="426f9c93-bf53-4f1a-ab38-9e39a5fbc6ac" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285001_752043_89821"/>
        <body>This capability is for the representation of the data that identify a requirement and versions of requirements.&lt;br/&gt; The concept of a 'requirement' in this context, relates chiefly to the exchange and sharing of data between requirements engineering applications such as those used in the systems engineering and related industrial domains.&lt;br/&gt; This capability also include the verification and validation used together for checking that a data meets requirements and that it fulfils its intended purpose. &lt;br/&gt;The figure below provides an overview of the capability. &lt;figuresysml&gt;&lt;id&gt;_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491291654_141462_96902&lt;/id&gt;Block Definition Diagram of the Requirement Management CTC&lt;/figuresysml&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>RequirementManagement</name>
      <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285089_918961_89898" xmi:uuid="7efbf5a3-5f5a-4d31-b6dc-0e2f3c0a9dbb" xmi:type="uml:Package">
