        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491291795_131267_97029" xmi:uuid="2ba1b4ab-2e9f-43d7-a4d0-c89785178613" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491348161_702833_136432" xmi:uuid="b7d31e33-64c4-4b40-b2ab-a1329a116454" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491291795_131267_97029"/>
            <body>A RequirementAssignment is an assignment of a Requirement (via a RequirementView) to an item (specified by RequirementAssignmentSelect) which is affected by the requirement. The meaning of the assignment can be specified using the ClassifiedAs attribute inherited from the AssignmentObject. &lt;example&gt;A requirement 'the vehicle shall have a maximum power output of at least 150BHP' could be assigned to the item which represents the vehicle's engine.&lt;/example&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>RequirementAssignment</name>
