        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491291815_384036_97031" xmi:uuid="62c04dae-4f31-4a87-8fb4-1e458f18ef5e" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491348397_217860_136559" xmi:uuid="bdb209d5-4ce9-499d-8b45-639107fc5b25" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491291815_384036_97031"/>
            <body>A RequirementTracingRelationship is a type of RequirementViewRelationship. It identifies a tracing relationship. &lt;example&gt;A requirement on the performance of a catalytic converter in a car can be traced from a more general emissions requirement. A requirement can trace to many other requirements and vice versa - this is achieved by creating multiple instances of the tracing relationship entity.&lt;/example&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>RequirementTracingRelationship</name>
