    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491284995_844162_89808" xmi:uuid="3e1333dd-d783-439f-927f-fd8ce79fe238" xmi:type="uml:Package">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285039_210771_89847" xmi:uuid="2814b1be-5e90-4625-a3f7-7f80e7f2cde4" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491284995_844162_89808"/>
        <body>This capability represents common information to be used such as:&lt;br/&gt; 1) The identification of product or activity data :&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;It allows for the identification of classes,&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Identifiers can be defined and put into hierarchical relationships, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Classification information can be assigned to identifiers. This capability enables the description of product or activity data. It allows for the description of classes, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Descriptors can be defined and put into hierarchical relationships, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Classification information can be assigned to descriptors.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; 2) The classification of product or activity data: &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt; it allows for the identification of classes, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;classes can be defined in a class system and put into hierarchical relationships, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Classification information can be assigned to product or activity data, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;the association of classes and product data can be characterized by property definitions.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; 3) The date and time: &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;a date and time can be used in combination with persons and organizations or directly associated with product data, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;a date and time information consists of simple calendar dates or time stamps more complex definitions like spans of time or events.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; 4) The specification of properties and their association with other product data like parts or documents: &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;a property is the definition of a special quality and can reflect physics or arbitrary, user defined measurements, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;a general pattern for instantiating property information is defined by this capability, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;properties can exist independently from their association with product or activity data, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;properties are defined globally and have a value associated, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;independent properties can be assigned to product data, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;for simple use cases, which do not require the full property concept, a simple property mechanism is provided. This allows for the association of a name value pair with product data.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; 5) The specification of environments&lt;br/&gt; 6) The specification of effectivities&lt;br/&gt; 7) The specification of conditions.&lt;br/&gt; The figure below provides an overview of the capability. &lt;figuresysml&gt;&lt;id&gt;_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491286087_318355_91010&lt;/id&gt;Overview of the Common Resources CTC&lt;/figuresysml&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>CommonResources</name>
      <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285023_892132_89846" xmi:uuid="1941226b-9bd1-4e8c-b27a-5a5d1ed3b91b" xmi:type="uml:Package">
