        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491287034_909886_92430" xmi:uuid="0a3826e4-4aac-4395-b338-6e76f6d643b0" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491305356_832726_109746" xmi:uuid="b6c093df-1d10-4cba-ac3a-9dbe501ceb80" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491287034_909886_92430"/>
            <body>A DateTimeAssignment is an assignment of point in time specified as a DateTimeString to an item (specified by DateTimeAssignmentSelect). The meaning of the assignment can be specified using the ClassifiedAs attribute inherited from the AssignmentObject. &lt;example&gt; If applied to an instance of Part with classification 'creation date', the DateTimeAssignment specifies the creation date of the part, tool, or raw material as a new object in the activity domain, and not the creation date of the instance of Part in a product management system.&lt;/example&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>DateTimeAssignment</name>
          <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491301235_385121_105392" xmi:uuid="2f238682-4703-49f8-9f08-4fa76dea8643" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
