        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491286983_408050_92408" xmi:uuid="2bf6e6d4-ec89-4200-afbd-d52ab57b2e64" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491304344_383952_108942" xmi:uuid="e9e19779-c688-44d6-a171-e21c0520cec1" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491286983_408050_92408"/>
            <body>A Class is a classification of an object which characterizes all objects of the same kind; such a classification is independent from the application of the classified object. &lt;example&gt; A fastener with subclasses, such as fastener with 2 or 3 fixture holes, a bracket with subclasses with 90 or 100 degrees bending angle, or screws with subclasses such as metal screws or machine screws are examples for Class. &lt;/example&gt; &lt;example&gt; For facilitating an effective part retrieval for slotted screws, several Class objects can be defined to classify screws: &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;A Class *1 with Description 'slotted screws' and three subclasses with the Descriptions *2: 'slotted cheese head screws - product grade A', *3: 'slotted pan head screws - product grade A', and *4: 'slotted countersunk flat head screws - product grade A'. &lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Each of the Class objects is based on a Class that further defines where the definition of the Class comes from. For Class *1 this is a company internal ExternalClassSystem for 'screw classes'. For the other Class objects these are ISO standardized ExternalClassSystem objects, namely for *2 'ISO 1207', for *3 'ISO 1580', and for *4 'ISO 2010'. &lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;The Class objects can be characterized further by ClassAttribute objects. According to ISO 1207, the Class *2 has the attributes *11 with Id 'd' and Description 'thread', *12 with Id 'l' and Description 'nominal length', *13 with Id 'mechanical properties' and Description 'property class', etc. The possible values 'M1.6', 'M2', ..., 'M10' for ClassAttribute *11 can be defined as PropertyValue objects in a set of the attribute allowedValues. The according specification is given as &lt;a&gt;&lt;path&gt;./4_info_reqs_CommonResources.htm#PropertyValue.Name&lt;/path&gt; Name&lt;/a&gt; of the PropertyValue. The PropertyValue refer as their definition to a PropertyDefinition with the PropertyType 'nominal metric thread diameter'. &lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;To identify the designation 'Cheese head screw ISO 1207 - M5 x 20 x 4.8', a subclass of Class *2 is defined with the same Description 'slotted cheese head screws ISO 1207 -M5 x 20 x 4.8' but with the values for ClassAttribute corresponding to *11 restricted to 'M5' only, to get just the M5 screws, corresponding to *12 restricted to value '20' only, and corresponding to *13 restricted to value '4.8' only (for steel according to ISO 898-1). &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; &lt;/example&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>Class</name>
          <ownedRule xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491304217_123751_108838" xmi:uuid="917a39a5-f2ba-4ec5-801b-3f79088d0c6c" xmi:type="uml:Constraint">
