        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491287352_982863_92663" xmi:uuid="4cfc2593-e7f4-4ee3-8c75-819e148e0340" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491311161_277051_114553" xmi:uuid="9b65c578-76f0-492c-9014-6a522ec34833" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491287352_982863_92663"/>
            <body>A ValueList is a type of PropertyValue with an ordered collection of PropertyValue objects. &lt;example&gt;A PropertyDefinition can be composed of different property values such as 'mass', 'speed', and 'age' which are altogether necessary in a given context. The ValueList collects all of them in a given order, such that each is identifiable by its index in the list.&lt;/example&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>ValueList</name>
          <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491308958_253231_112758" xmi:uuid="3fabca0e-3392-49d5-a00c-b6650fe3e721" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
