        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491287059_187609_92450" xmi:uuid="57554be7-b9da-4b16-87fc-db5cfe91efa1" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491305873_748785_110161" xmi:uuid="76d2a0bf-a291-41d6-83cc-93328d57d5e7" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491287059_187609_92450"/>
            <body>An Effectivity is an identification of the valid use of an aspect of product data tracked by date, event, serial number or lot size. &lt;note&gt; An instance of Effectivity can define a period of ineffectivity or invalid use, if it is referred to by an instance of EffectivityAssignment with EffectivityIndication set to 'false'.&lt;/note&gt; An Effectivity can 'inherit' its interval from another Effectivity through an EffectivityRelationship with &lt;a&gt;&lt;path&gt;./4_info_reqs_CommonResources.htm#EffectivityRelationship.RelationType&lt;/path&gt; RelationType&lt;/a&gt; 'inheritance effectivity relationship'. If a 'start' and no 'end' is specified, the period is then added to 'start' in order to get the actual 'end' of the effectivity or ineffectivity.</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>Effectivity</name>
          <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491305755_147887_110070" xmi:uuid="068764ad-ef03-423b-9d50-f08bc8bdd95c" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
