        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491286823_588879_92112" xmi:uuid="785da332-68fc-48d6-b3af-fec6590f925f" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491302841_818904_107138" xmi:uuid="4e6597ca-582b-478d-923d-8dad8f3e609a" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491286823_588879_92112"/>
            <body>The classification information can be provided by several ways: &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt;by a simple class string; &lt;example&gt; A string 'company' specifies that an Organization is a company.&lt;/example&gt; &lt;note&gt;For the permissive list of values, this notion will be used.&lt;/note&gt;&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;by the definition of an explicit class; &lt;example&gt; A class with id 'company' classifies all Organization objects which are companies. The Class object allows for additional information like a description.&lt;/example&gt;&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;by the definition of an external class; &lt;example&gt; The information, that an Organization is classified as a company, is defined in an ExternalClass which is referenced by id and source.&lt;/example&gt;&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;by the definition of an external owl class. &lt;example&gt; The information, that an Organization is classified as a company, is defined in an ExternalOwlClass which is referenced by a URI.&lt;/example&gt;&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>ClassSelect</name>
          <isAbstract>true</isAbstract>
          <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677509423453_373821_76323" xmi:uuid="08f1f778-f05c-4b5f-89b9-d7a1b2141dca" xmi:type="uml:Port">
            <name>classSelect</name>
            <visibility>public</visibility>
            <type href="../../../Core_model/CommonResources/CommonResources.xmi#_ClassSelect"/>
            <aggregation>composite</aggregation>
          </ownedAttribute>
        </packagedElement>
