        </packagedElement>
        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491287032_806271_92429" xmi:uuid="c7d372a1-cf9b-4226-adc3-1c55e07f14d8" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491305262_988411_109665" xmi:uuid="41465226-726f-4a9e-a19b-d4e4a5e248fc" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491287032_806271_92429"/>
            <body>A DatedEffectivity is a specialization of Effectivity for which the domain of applicability is defined as an interval of time bounded by dates or events. The time bounds are defined by its inherited attributes StartDefinition or EndDefinition. The interval can be open-ended. &lt;example&gt;Events can be used to bound a DatedEffectivity period, at planning phase.&lt;/example&gt; Depending on which of the StartDefinition and EndDefinition attributes are specified, the actual domain of time defined by a DatedEffectivity is: &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;the time interval between the start and end date or event; &lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;the open time interval that starts at the start date or event; &lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;the open time interval that ends at the end date or event (in this case the start is unknown). &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; If the EndDefinition is an event that actually identifies a point in time that comes before the StartDefinition, then the actual domain of effectivity is empty.</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>DatedEffectivity</name>
          <ownedRule xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491305239_752795_109639" xmi:uuid="1a9efadc-d58f-4261-9bdb-8fd563b23595" xmi:type="uml:Constraint">
            <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491380449_133535_159501" xmi:uuid="b3628a10-a37e-467b-bf40-9fce02289b35" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
              <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491305239_752795_109639"/>
              <body>the StartDefinition shall be before the EndDefinition.</body>
            </ownedComment>
            <name>WR2</name>
            <constrainedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491287032_806271_92429"/>
            <specification xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491380449_393417_159500" xmi:uuid="db6ee7d8-f501-4dc7-9435-3a45a9c27321" xmi:type="uml:OpaqueExpression">
              <body>self.StartDefinition &lt; self.EndDefinition</body>
              <language>OCL2.0</language>
            </specification>
          </ownedRule>
          <ownedRule xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491305239_264571_109640" xmi:uuid="809d38fc-7781-4212-b58a-caac786ac83f" xmi:type="uml:Constraint">
            <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491380449_239056_159503" xmi:uuid="524a1a9b-5166-4c6a-9df8-d47d737e6116" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
              <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491305239_264571_109640"/>
              <body> at least one of the attributes StartDefinition or EndDefinition shall be set.</body>
            </ownedComment>
            <name>WR1</name>
            <constrainedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491287032_806271_92429"/>
            <specification xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491380449_823803_159502" xmi:uuid="c6664efd-2131-40ae-9ccf-024fc0f96461" xmi:type="uml:OpaqueExpression">
              <body>not(self.StartDefinition.oclIsUndefined()) or not(self.EndDefinition.oclIsUndefined())</body>
              <language>OCL2.0</language>
            </specification>
          </ownedRule>
          <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491305238_202232_109637" xmi:uuid="e4cd05e6-4340-4cbc-8687-4b18604bf600" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
            <general xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491287059_187609_92450"/>
          </generalization>
          <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491303344_979900_107973" xmi:uuid="948f98f5-642d-4848-b2fc-bde1296656e1" xmi:type="uml:Property">
            <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491377959_965972_156743" xmi:uuid="5632f2cf-23f5-4ee8-8ae0-8a2944720149" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
              <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491303344_979900_107973"/>
              <body> the item (specified by EventOrDateSelect) that defines the upper bound of the interval of applicability. The value of this attribute need not be specified. If the value for this attribute is not specified, the interval of applicability has no upper bound.</body>
            </ownedComment>
            <name>EndDefinition</name>
            <visibility>public</visibility>
            <type xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491286850_433873_92119"/>
            <lowerValue xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491377959_471699_156744" xmi:uuid="0d41329c-37c9-4e07-b6d3-90686f8a8ad5" xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger"/>
            <association xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491286907_554610_92196"/>
          </ownedAttribute>
          <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491303348_912083_107978" xmi:uuid="18d34dd3-062f-4a3d-9be6-94b2cf573ebe" xmi:type="uml:Property">
            <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491377961_730832_156757" xmi:uuid="0f9c1c2e-9439-47a8-9d22-651b86159207" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
              <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491303348_912083_107978"/>
              <body> the item (specified by EventOrDateSelect) that defines the lower bound of the interval of applicability. The value of this attribute need not be specified.</body>
            </ownedComment>
            <name>StartDefinition</name>
            <visibility>public</visibility>
            <type xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491286850_433873_92119"/>
            <lowerValue xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491377962_473916_156758" xmi:uuid="2d314f47-b0e3-46d5-b7a2-188f223d670d" xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger"/>
