        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491286665_216789_91841" xmi:uuid="d4dfcade-c6da-4d0f-9441-014fac4358b7" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491300485_965067_104648" xmi:uuid="dd75c1dc-e275-4465-95cc-2bc0e9f77572" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491286665_216789_91841"/>
            <body>A ConditionalConfiguration is a type of ConditionalEffectivity and represents an association of a SpecificationConditionAssignment or a SpecificationAssignment object with a design or with a process in order to define a valid usage of it in the context of a certain ProductClass. &lt;note&gt; The semantics of the kind of association is defined by the attributes ConfigurationType and InheritanceType. &lt;/note&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>ConditionalConfiguration</name>
