        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491287066_641041_92451" xmi:uuid="e09543ad-3eb6-49d8-aa91-cf4aa113206d" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491306060_918845_110323" xmi:uuid="3eb28b86-fd3e-4a96-943e-e9a1671af95b" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491287066_641041_92451"/>
            <body>An EffectivityAssignment is an assignment of an Effectivity to an item (specified by EffectivityAssignmentSelect) whose effectivity is controlled by the assigned Effectivity. The association of an Effectivity to product or activity data does not imply any statement concerning effectivity outside of the specified interval. The same applies in the absence of any AssignedEffectivity, that is, no statement concerning effectivity is implied.</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>EffectivityAssignment</name>
