        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491292269_937037_97428" xmi:uuid="261dc43b-ba34-4d0d-8109-d445fe29ff1f" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491352078_958484_138275" xmi:uuid="24a47bea-37ac-44ce-90c9-10c9cc83c2d3" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491292269_937037_97428"/>
            <body>A RequiredResourceAssignment is an assignment of a RequiredResource to an item (specified by RequiredResourceAssignmentSelect) that requires the resource. The meaning of the assignment can be specified using the ClassifiedAs attribute inherited from the AssignmentObject. &lt;example&gt;Task, task step, activity, activity method, organization are examples of entities to which the resource requirement statement could be related.&lt;/example&gt; &lt;example&gt;The assignment can be classified as "required by".&lt;/example&gt; &lt;note&gt;An association between a required resource and actions that are needed prior to its usage.&lt;/note&gt; &lt;example&gt;A resource required by the activity "12" needs to be calibrated prior to usage. The calibration activity "21" is associated with the same required resource.&lt;/example&gt; &lt;example&gt;A resource required by the task "123" needs to be disposed after its usage. This disposal task "456" is associated with the same required resource.&lt;/example&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>RequiredResourceAssignment</name>
          <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491303021_680159_107510" xmi:uuid="009b0262-3252-41b8-b60a-32b6322993e7" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
