        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491292287_344607_97434" xmi:uuid="d353c320-8d92-43ea-a543-c3e4fd7c8946" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491352537_850189_138471" xmi:uuid="105683a3-38e7-46d6-a817-d159d9477079" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491292287_344607_97434"/>
            <body>A ResourceEvent is an abstract generalization of instances that represents an event or action that affects the balance or availability of a managed resource. &lt;note&gt;Only non-abstract specializations of the ResourceEvent can be instantiated.&lt;/note&gt; A ResourceEvent is the role of a resource event is determined by which is specified by the ClassifiedAs property. &lt;example&gt;A resource event can be classified as "Planned" or "Actual".&lt;/example&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>ResourceEvent</name>
