    </packagedElement>
    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285003_997362_89826" xmi:uuid="54a83eb0-3cd6-4be1-b8b3-e3cfcb7597ff" xmi:type="uml:Package">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285106_884325_89915" xmi:uuid="97334955-41fa-4255-8ee3-0f83b825ac1c" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285003_997362_89826"/>
        <body>This capability is for the representation of the data that specifies task methods, that is the method specified for a particular activity. The task method specifications can then be referenced from schedules and in recording activities that have been undertaken. &lt;br/&gt;The figure below provides an overview of the capability. &lt;figuresysml&gt;&lt;id&gt;_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491293166_89134_98044&lt;/id&gt;Block Definition Diagram of the TaskDescription CTC&lt;/figuresysml&gt; TaskElements can have the following characteristics: &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;A Task method is the combination of something to be achieved and, optionally, a way to achieve it.The same result can be achieved through more than one method;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A Task method can be defined as simple text or as a processable structure using repeats, sequences and decision points;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A Task method can be associated with pre and post states.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; The following are not enabled directly by this capability alone but are enabled by capabilities that use this module: &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;A Task method can be associated with the resources required to do it.The quantity of resource and the probability that it is needed can be specified;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A resource can optionally be linked to specific stages within a task method as well as to the overall task method;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The output from a task method can be specified, with quantities and probabilities of occurrence.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; These capabilities are achieved by linking this capability to the application modules used to define resources, locations, conditions and justifications. Further details are presented below. The capabilities provided by this capability include: &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;the identification of resources required by tasks;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;the identification of products to which tasks are assigned;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;the association of properties with task specifications;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;the association of dates, times, people, approvals and other management data with task specifications;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;the specification of conditions under which a task falls due;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;the association of a justification and a probability with a task assignment to a product, or a resource assignment to a task;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;the association of a location with a task or resource;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;the association of a task specification with the requirement from which it derived.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; The kinds of resources that can be defined for a task include: &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;products, either types of product or individual products;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;people, types of people, organizations, types of organization, or positions within organizations;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;documents and information held as files. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; The resource allocation, and the assignment of the task to a product, can be qualified by a condition, a justification or a probability. The conditions can be stated in terms of the state of the product, its age, its usage or any other parameter. Justifications can be related to supporting data or documents. A required resource can be related to allocation. </body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>TaskDescription</name>
      <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285103_6991_89914" xmi:uuid="4e5e2c8a-e78a-4c1f-b58a-3cb0ed4e53d3" xmi:type="uml:Package">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491293497_576055_98315" xmi:uuid="63c8aa22-9971-4640-a114-94a23a4eb872" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285103_6991_89914"/>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>ModelElements</name>
