      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285080_692258_89889" xmi:uuid="8c4796e0-7fbd-4451-b557-7d71fde46b88" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285000_633946_89819"/>
        <body>This capability is for the representation of products with a large number of variants. &lt;example&gt;Examples for aircraft products are propeller aircrafts, jet aircrafts, rocket-powered aircrafts, or engines or components of these products. Examples for automotive products are passenger cars, trucks, busses, or engines or components of these products. &lt;/example&gt; Because of the large number of variants there is no unique identification for each of the variants that could be produced. The main concepts that are used to handle this large number of variants are the following: &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt;product classes are used to identify sets of similar products to be offered to the market;&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;specifications are used to describe characteristics of the products;&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;specification categories are used to group similar characteristics of the products;&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;specification expressions are used to control the usage of a part within a product and to represent conditions for product classes.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt; This capability provides mechanisms to identify a single manufacturable product out of a large number of variants. The main concepts that are used to handle this identification of a single manufacturable product are the following:&lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt;Product configurations are used to identify a manufacturable product out of a possibly large number of variants of a product class by its associated specifications without having an explicit representation of the product, such as a customer order for a car;&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Product design association (ProductDesignAssociation) is used to associate an implicit representation of a manufacturable product (ProductConfiguration) with its explicit representation (PartVersion);&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Manufacturing configuration is used to specify the validity of occurrences of parts (Occurrence) with regard to manufacturing aspects in the context of an implicit as well as an explicit representation of a manufacturable product (ProductConfiguration, PartVersion);&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Configurations (ProductConfiguration) are used to configure part occurrences, alternative solutions, breakdown elements, and process plans in the context of the conditions (SpecificationConditionAssignment, SpecificationAssignment) under which they are valid. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; &lt;br/&gt;The figure below provides an overview of the capability. &lt;figuresysml&gt;&lt;id&gt;_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491290991_33896_96256&lt;/id&gt;Block Definition Diagram of the Product Specification and Configuration CTC&lt;/figuresysml&gt; </body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>ProductSpecificationAndConfiguration</name>
      <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285075_657228_89885" xmi:uuid="2d78cee0-136c-4a3f-bfe4-f87d4654d077" xmi:type="uml:Package">
        <name>Diagrams</name>
      </packagedElement>
      <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285076_491160_89886" xmi:uuid="74058b97-fe7c-4cce-9f67-a62b305b6835" xmi:type="uml:Package">
        <name>ModelElements</name>
        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491291180_829105_96312" xmi:uuid="05c2d5d8-6078-48bd-bf26-c3791153c00a" xmi:type="uml:Association">
          <memberEnd xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491344936_755395_134676"/>
          <memberEnd xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491342673_303919_133588"/>
          <ownedEnd xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491344936_755395_134676" xmi:uuid="b172f009-07e1-4224-bb87-aadc8a682929" xmi:type="uml:Property">
            <type xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491291060_176136_96281"/>
            <lowerValue xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491437467_903918_193812" xmi:uuid="a8e1e54f-ac1b-41ec-a132-a05f2399b0de" xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger"/>
            <association xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491291180_829105_96312"/>
          </ownedEnd>
        </packagedElement>
        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491291172_319020_96294" xmi:uuid="0751546e-3d2f-4039-b87a-70fa607d0bc8" xmi:type="uml:Association">
          <memberEnd xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491341897_991956_133211"/>
          <memberEnd xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491342191_652025_133336"/>
        </packagedElement>
        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491291177_340336_96306" xmi:uuid="09251cd4-0e8b-463c-8abf-ce9b23dc0735" xmi:type="uml:Association">
          <memberEnd xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491344927_171657_134670"/>
          <memberEnd xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491343352_448528_133911"/>
          <ownedEnd xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491344927_171657_134670" xmi:uuid="c5479097-2018-4135-ad64-d4aae27bb80e" xmi:type="uml:Property">
            <type xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491291090_805214_96284"/>
            <lowerValue xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491437463_925706_193800" xmi:uuid="91045ec5-e319-4c17-b7fe-17e69709b3b4" xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger"/>
            <association xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491291177_340336_96306"/>
          </ownedEnd>
        </packagedElement>
        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491291029_793568_96278" xmi:uuid="11811b3f-e000-46d3-ad83-138f4c46a65e" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491342172_235782_133328" xmi:uuid="35c40d37-a773-42d2-8591-26999b768ad5" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491291029_793568_96278"/>
            <body>A ProductConfiguration is a manufacturable object or expected as so. A ProductConfiguration is defined with respect to the ProductClass from which it is a member. &lt;note&gt; The kind of product that is to be manufactured from the data of the ProductConfiguration, is defined by the ProductConcept to which the ProductConfiguration belongs. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; The intent of ProductConfiguration is the identification of one manufacturable object whereas the intent of ProductClass is the gathering of products with similar characteristics. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;example&gt; A ProductConfiguration that is associated with a ProductClass that identifies a family of diesel engines is intended to lead to the manufacture of a specific case of diesel engine, and the ProductConfiguration that is associated with a ProductClass that identifies a car family will lead to the manufacture of a car. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;note&gt; The entity ProductConfiguration corresponds to the concept of configuration item defined, in some configuration management standards, as an item subject to configuration management. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;example&gt; A ProductConfiguration can represent a component of a contracted product, onto which severe safety rules apply and for which configuration management is therefore rigorously applied. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;note&gt; A ProductConfiguration can identify a variation of a ProductClass, an entire ProductClass, or some portion thereof. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; A ProductConfiguration can be established prior to the existence of a corresponding product.&lt;/note&gt; For a ProductConfiguration one or more additional Specification objects can be specified. In this case they enhance the characterization provided for the associated ProductClass. &lt;note&gt; The actual set of Specification objects for a ProductConfiguration are obtained by the union of DefiningSpecifications and of the Specification objects related to the &lt;a&gt;&lt;path&gt;./4_info_reqs_ProductSpecificationAndConfiguration.htm#SpecificationAssignment.AssignedTo&lt;/path&gt; AssignedTo&lt;/a&gt; through a SpecificationAssignment or a SpecificationConditionAssignment with AssociationType 'identification' or 'non-replaceable standard'. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; The specification of a ProductConfiguration can be incomplete: there cannot be in DefiningSpecifications any instance of Specification for some SpecificationCategory declared as mandatory for the &lt;a&gt;&lt;path&gt;./4_info_reqs_ProductSpecificationAndConfiguration.htm#SpecificationAssignment.AssignedTo&lt;/path&gt; AssignedTo&lt;/a&gt;. For these SpecificationCategory objects any Specification available in the context of the &lt;a&gt;&lt;path&gt;./4_info_reqs_ProductSpecificationAndConfiguration.htm#SpecificationAssignment.AssignedTo&lt;/path&gt; AssignedTo&lt;/a&gt; is considered as valid for the manufacturing of the product characterized by the considered SpecificationAssignment. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;example&gt; If the colour is not specified for a given car family, the vehicle resulting from the realization of a ProductConfiguration associated to the ProductClass representing the car family can be without paint or painted in any available colour. &lt;/example&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>ProductConfiguration</name>
