        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491291141_948333_96289" xmi:uuid="9216f734-be86-4182-bbff-3abcf6e1e4f9" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491344340_189248_134394" xmi:uuid="18155c29-3307-4220-8137-eac01d410e2f" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491291141_948333_96289"/>
            <body>A SpecificationCategoryAssignment is an assignment of a SpecificationCategory to a ProductClass. Additionally, this assignment specifies if the usage of one or more Specification objects belonging to this SpecificationCategory, is mandatory or optional for all products of that ProductClass. The meaning of the assignment can be specified using the ClassifiedAs attribute inherited from the AssignmentObject. &lt;note&gt; The assignment of a SpecificationCategory to a ProductClass does not replace the association of single members of the SpecificationCategory to the ProductClass. &lt;/note&gt;</body>
