          <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491321739_18581_121378" xmi:uuid="e81d1a17-cf39-4ec3-bb1f-8fbec44f160f" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
            <general xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491288814_615872_94197"/>
          </generalization>
          <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491342343_337021_133419" xmi:uuid="b5153ac6-27f1-4948-908f-fc834f2eeba4" xmi:type="uml:Property">
            <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491434165_825054_191736" xmi:uuid="06672ae9-730a-493f-82f7-4f08a03e2093" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
              <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491342343_337021_133419"/>
              <body> the level of the ProductClass in a hierarchical structure of ProductClass objects. This information is defined by reference data. The ReferenceData tab provides definitions of the Reference Data currently standardized for ProductClass. The value of this attribute need not be specified. &lt;example&gt; A high level ProductClass (LevelType = 'enterprise') can be used to define all SpecificationCategory and Specification objects for all ProductClass objects of an enterprise with several brands and companies. A second level ProductClass (LevelType = 'platform') can be used to group all products that are based on the same technical concept (platform); these products can belong to different brands. A third level ProductClass (LevelType = 'car family') can be used to group all products that have a common base and a fixed set of characteristics (specification categories). A fourth level ProductClass (LevelType = 'car type') can represent products that are offered to the market; this level of ProductClass can be defined by the marketing department. A set of specifications sufficient to produce the car is associated with its ProductClass. Within this association, a distinction is made between standard characteristics (such as number of doors) and options that have to be chosen (such as outside colour) or that can be chosen by the customer (such as radio).&lt;/example&gt; </body>
            </ownedComment>
            <name>LevelType</name>
            <visibility>public</visibility>
            <type xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491286823_588879_92112"/>
            <lowerValue xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491434166_257037_191737" xmi:uuid="13aef49f-b730-464a-b502-40ccd4a4bf4f" xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger"/>
            <association xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491291198_728120_96346"/>
          </ownedAttribute>
