        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491289751_808469_94993" xmi:uuid="fd446b1a-fdb9-42ee-990c-03f667cdae16" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491331313_531305_127215" xmi:uuid="67cff494-ec8a-4cfc-9949-2ef3194f6ebe" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491289751_808469_94993"/>
            <body>A Scheme provides the identification and description of an intended course of action to accomplish an objective. A Scheme allows for the ordering of entries. Dates and times can be specified for entries and time intervals between entries. &lt;note&gt;A Scheme can be classified as a Plan or a Schedule, and it can be further classified into specific types of Plans or Schedules.&lt;/note&gt; &lt;example&gt;Acquisition plan, Maintenance plan, and Resource schedule are examples of schemes.&lt;/example&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>Scheme</name>
          <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1701851419223_238456_85622" xmi:uuid="01b00463-20ad-40f2-bb75-8ecb2d55810d" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
