      <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285061_56936_89870" xmi:uuid="fb9b5e5c-d1b2-46a7-b3f6-9bafbe42ef10" xmi:type="uml:Package">
        <name>Diagrams</name>
      </packagedElement>
    </packagedElement>
    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491284997_358056_89813" xmi:uuid="add70cf0-0a0a-4c5c-8566-b30b765ef576" xmi:type="uml:Package">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285060_799096_89866" xmi:uuid="5d6d7424-c5c0-482d-9330-75260eea9683" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491284997_358056_89813"/>
        <body>This capability is for the representation of the data that identify a Message and an Envelope. Message is a collection of information, brought together by an originator (the message definer) for some specific purpose, generally the fulfilment of a process. An Envelope is the historical record of the transmissions of a Message. &lt;br/&gt;The figure below provides an overview of the capability. &lt;figuresysml&gt;&lt;id&gt;_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491289371_243422_94649&lt;/id&gt;Block Definition Diagram of the Message CTC&lt;/figuresysml&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>Message</name>
      <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285059_678292_89865" xmi:uuid="7ddd8257-df55-4e1c-bea0-8a94ebf7f76a" xmi:type="uml:Package">
        <name>ModelElements</name>
        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491289462_154266_94715" xmi:uuid="081541c5-65ea-4adf-b433-9fddb5a891c8" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491329542_353153_126302" xmi:uuid="841a0b93-8f18-434e-b240-853d3f7ec381" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491289462_154266_94715"/>
            <body>A Message is a collection of information, brought together by an originator (the message definer) for some specific purpose, generally the fulfilment of a process. A Message is an historical record, intended to be sent using an Envelope and in consequence, is not versioned. Once a Message is sent to a first addressee, it shall not be changed. However it shall not remain unsent, since that is to confuse its functions and therefore its meaning with other entities such as Document.&lt;note&gt; The same Message can be sent several times using different Envelope objects.&lt;/note&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>Message</name>
          <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491328180_836073_125450" xmi:uuid="27cd256f-d023-4f13-b822-4b3df31a7c58" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
            <general xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491289267_929523_94546"/>
          </generalization>
          <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491328325_573462_125556" xmi:uuid="3d26abcf-0e3c-4d29-80dc-402b0f49ec4f" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
            <general xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491289280_769901_94550"/>
          </generalization>
          <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491329424_546681_126230" xmi:uuid="be4b3263-cb1a-4b0f-ba52-848a2d9df2d8" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
            <general xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491289637_3891_94862"/>
          </generalization>
          <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491298326_503098_103625" xmi:uuid="e36157cc-2bf2-4467-b4f8-353921338b1f" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
