        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285491_591181_90182" xmi:uuid="b4204b99-b453-4eed-b601-22b3fb78da5a" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491295039_710833_100038" xmi:uuid="491573ee-2c0d-4429-88df-fb1b121afa25" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285491_591181_90182"/>
            <body>An AnalysisDisciplineDefinition is a definition or view of an AnalysisVersion taken from the perspective of the analysing organization. The AnalysisDisciplineDefinition is controlled by the analysing organization. The entity can be used to capture the definition of a specific version of an Analysis at any intermediate stage of its development where the definition is not formally released by an organization at the Analysis version level. It can be used to capture the various stages in the definition cycle of a product. If the Analysis is explicitly represented by a model, then the model is referenced using the DefinitionalRepresentations attribute.</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>AnalysisDisciplineDefinition</name>
