    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491284994_769012_89806" xmi:uuid="bb10aeb1-d6bd-4c7a-8dfc-78fa58bb94c8" xmi:type="uml:Package">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285018_559117_89839" xmi:uuid="7dbe1fae-53a9-4fb3-855d-ab179cc7163e" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491284994_769012_89806"/>
        <body>This capability enables the representation of parent-child structures, so-called breakdowns. A breakdown consists of breakdown elements. Different types of breakdowns and breakdown elements are distinguished, such as functional and physical. Breakdowns can be views of actual product structures with relations to only some of their constituents.&lt;br/&gt; This capability also enables the representation of alternative solutions, such as final, supplier or technical solutions. These are implementations of functional and physical breakdown elements.&lt;br/&gt; Finally, part occurrences, that is, occurrences of parts in certain locations, can be associated with breakdown elements by means of this capability.&lt;br/&gt; The figure below provides an overview of the capability. &lt;br/&gt;&lt;figuresysml&gt;&lt;id&gt;_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285521_927154_90284&lt;/id&gt;Block Definition Diagram of the Breakdown CTC&lt;/figuresysml&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>Breakdown</name>
      <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285011_952787_89836" xmi:uuid="56470d3d-97c5-4c6d-82f5-ce12cc9ed629" xmi:type="uml:Package">
        <name>Diagrams</name>
      </packagedElement>
