        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491292695_386568_97730" xmi:uuid="14de5175-58d9-4fb8-8050-0e401fc01c2b" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491356717_921208_140438" xmi:uuid="ba3b4054-5edc-473a-b33b-0ee9fbea68c1" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491292695_386568_97730"/>
            <body>A RiskConsequence is a specialization of RiskView and specifies the outcome of the risk occurring. &lt;note&gt;There can be one or more consequences of a risk occurring.&lt;/note&gt; &lt;note&gt;Consequences can range from positive to negative. However, consequences are always negative for safety aspects.&lt;/note&gt; &lt;note&gt;Consequences can be expressed qualitatively or quantitatively.&lt;/note&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>RiskConsequence</name>
          <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491356107_946086_140126" xmi:uuid="5b7cdc0b-7b95-4913-b4e8-a116f8c052ae" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
