        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491292594_61046_97674" xmi:uuid="e67e9dc0-082e-44a1-b60f-fc15f01f72ea" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491355689_565727_139965" xmi:uuid="7bfb7c41-b675-4fc3-a8db-1735e5cea02c" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491292594_61046_97674"/>
            <body>A Risk is the potential for realization of unwanted negative consequences of an event. &lt;note&gt;ISO Guide 73:2009 defines "risk" as the effect of uncertainty on objectives.&lt;/note&gt; &lt;note&gt;A risk can also have a possible positive outcome. In such cases it is often referred to as an opportunity or reward.&lt;/note&gt; &lt;note&gt;ISO/IEC Guide 51:2014 defines risk as the combination of the probability of occurrence of harm and the severity of that harm.&lt;/note&gt; &lt;note&gt;In the safety field, risk management is focused on prevention and mitigation of harm.&lt;/note&gt; &lt;example&gt;'Line shutdown' is an example of Risk in the context of a manufacturing system's reliability.&lt;/example&gt; &lt;example&gt;'Transportation jam-up', 'customer anger', 'collateral damage', and 'greater susceptibility to interruption of supply during crises' are all examples of Risk.&lt;/example&gt; &lt;example&gt;'Privacy risk' and 'security risk' are examples of Risk for the telecommunications industry.&lt;/example&gt; &lt;example&gt;Timing such as 'premature rejection' and 'premature commitment' are other examples of Risk.&lt;/example&gt; </body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>Risk</name>
