            <body>An Approval is a judgement and formal confirmation of the quality of those product or activity data that are subject of the Approval. An Approval represents a statement made by technical personnel or management personnel whether certain requirements are met. The absence of approval information does not imply any approval status by default. &lt;note&gt; Approval purposes are defined within a given life-cycle stage view and are typically dependent upon the approval cycles within an individual business process. For each defined purpose, generally there is a defined sequence of values for the status, usually leading towards the status value 'approved' indicating achievement of the specific purpose.&lt;/note&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>Approval</name>
