        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491289032_864421_94378" xmi:uuid="e93db7d4-faed-435b-b0c7-b1808ea4e111" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491324810_89876_123280" xmi:uuid="88c914e0-111e-4f25-ac98-a12bd8ad12c2" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491289032_864421_94378"/>
            <body>An InformationRight is a definition of what can or cannot be done with an item of information in the sense of legal rights and obligations. &lt;example&gt; Copyright is an InformationRight. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;example&gt; For the purposes of developing a new system, details of government furnished equipment can be made available to a specific project team. The team can copy and use the information internally, but cannot pass it on, either to a third part, or to another team, and has to destroy the information at the end of the contract. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;note&gt; The following additional data can be assigned to an InformationRight: InformationUsageRight.&lt;/note&gt; </body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>InformationRight</name>
          <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491324658_604325_123192" xmi:uuid="0a495d12-527d-4ced-9112-c162962bbb20" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
