        </packagedElement>
        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491292825_260114_97837" xmi:uuid="0db25563-04ac-4126-b5ec-110114b3bc51" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491358107_800372_141028" xmi:uuid="b80961f8-79ef-4d85-9be2-f1f1a127afa6" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491292825_260114_97837"/>
            <body>A Slot represents the position in which a part is or can be attached. &lt;example&gt;A fast jet aircraft has two engines. These engines are removable and interchangeable between individual aircraft. An attachment slot represents each installation position for an engine so as to ensure that an accurate record is maintained of which engines fly in which pairing on which aircraft for how many hours. A rack has several shelfs, where PCB-cards can be installed. Each position/shelf is considered a slot. The PCB-cards are in this case considered as parts.&lt;/example&gt; </body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>Slot</name>
