        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491288041_561787_93342" xmi:uuid="1a31eeef-aa3f-4501-b53c-b5be0d6ee2d1" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491317790_265686_119180" xmi:uuid="1e06002c-9242-46ba-930e-7aa4cbbbf8cd" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491288041_561787_93342"/>
            <body>An InterfaceDefinitionFor is an association between an InterfaceSpecificationView and an item (specified by InterfaceDefinitionForSelect) that conforms to the specification. &lt;example&gt;The infrared transmitter in a television remote control conforms to the specification that has the identifier 2345/XYZ/001. An instance of the InterfaceDefinitionFor entity data type is necessary to identify this association.&lt;/example&gt; </body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>InterfaceDefinitionFor</name>
