        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491288029_852358_93340" xmi:uuid="5225213c-2603-4554-bedf-afa5f2f6e5b3" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491317634_978677_119079" xmi:uuid="b804df15-3ebc-4bf1-86ba-85afb3d63f4c" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491288029_852358_93340"/>
            <body>An InterfaceDefinitionConnection is an interconnection between a pair of views (specified by InterfaceDefinitionConnectionSelect). &lt;example&gt;A socket in the wall provides access to the domestic electricity supply. An appliance such as a television has a power lead and plug that fits into the socket. An instance of the InterfaceDefinitionConnection entity data type identifies this fitting of the plug into the socket.&lt;/example&gt; </body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>InterfaceDefinitionConnection</name>
