        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491293324_264493_98192" xmi:uuid="a55689f2-b1ef-4182-8cf7-a499f7d34f5f" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491362630_813802_142867" xmi:uuid="7e4b94e7-e815-41c5-becc-522928e54c72" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491293324_264493_98192"/>
            <body>An ActivityMethodRealization is a specialization of an AssociationObject. It is a further specification of how an activity method is to be performed with the ActivityMethod. &lt;note&gt;More than one specification can be associated with the same ActivityMethod.&lt;/note&gt; &lt;example&gt;For a given planned activity there can be a task specification, a statement of how task performance is to be logged and a schedule that all apply.&lt;/example&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>ActivityMethodRealization</name>
