    </packagedElement>
    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491284999_632928_89817" xmi:uuid="f15469e9-9664-4107-b8ab-3471869dda2a" xmi:type="uml:Package">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285068_413680_89879" xmi:uuid="3d791828-e8d0-4057-8c53-046bbfe13ed8" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491284999_632928_89817"/>
        <body>The Probability capability allows for the assignment of probability distributions to numerical values or random variables. &lt;br/&gt;The figure below provides an overview of the capability. &lt;figuresysml&gt;&lt;id&gt;_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491290289_273225_95568&lt;/id&gt;Block Definition Diagram of the Probability CTC&lt;/figuresysml&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>Probability</name>
      <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491285068_158371_89878" xmi:uuid="01bac98e-feaa-4db2-94bf-e4a7a1f5b6fd" xmi:type="uml:Package">
        <name>ModelElements</name>
        <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491290321_919993_95613" xmi:uuid="25f7be31-141f-4eb3-abf1-38c1c353ac31" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491335904_612856_130048" xmi:uuid="44ea29f0-07f6-4f70-9612-0994e3728586" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491290321_919993_95613"/>
            <body>A ParameterizedDistribution is a specialization of ProbabilityDistribution that is used to link a named probability distribution to the parameters that define it. &lt;note&gt; The ParameterizationName of this entity is used to discriminate between alternative parameterizations of the same distribution.&lt;/note&gt; &lt;note&gt; To calculate a value using a ParameterizedDistribution it is necessary to know the general distribution function, the value of the distribution function parameters, and the specific random variable value for which the probability evaluation is required. The ProbabilityDistribution module does not define the formula for the distribution function, and it is assumed that this is defined externally, either through reference information or via a "formula" module. This entity provides the distribution function parameters. &lt;/note&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <name>ParameterizedDistribution</name>
          <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491335875_840947_130023" xmi:uuid="4ad41b6c-4bcb-4f35-8810-10438367f811" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
            <general xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491290323_455612_95614"/>
          </generalization>
          <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491335910_362902_130051" xmi:uuid="e576c9ae-91b7-43b7-aedb-6e1832c6da94" xmi:type="uml:Property">
            <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491417002_578261_186878" xmi:uuid="af4098c6-0c7a-42ee-be78-df6ca129f551" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
              <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491335910_362902_130051"/>
              <body>the list of parameters used in the parameterization. The value of this attribute need not be specified. &lt;note&gt; In many distributions there is a trivial relationship between the mean and variance for the distribution. In such a case it is not necessary to list the parameters. &lt;/note&gt;</body>
            </ownedComment>
            <name>HasParameters</name>
            <visibility>public</visibility>
            <type xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491287157_236804_92523"/>
            <lowerValue xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491417003_951936_186879" xmi:uuid="9c3afe17-c771-4256-af59-a2aeb4491534" xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger"/>
            <upperValue xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491417001_429389_186877" xmi:uuid="1cb2815b-31e9-4a79-bf81-cdfd5122d4de" xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
              <value>*</value>
            </upperValue>
            <association xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491290331_310015_95624"/>
          </ownedAttribute>
          <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491335912_422685_130052" xmi:uuid="e8183ff8-79d2-4daa-8ddd-076708616c3d" xmi:type="uml:Property">
            <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491417004_793140_186882" xmi:uuid="d5291f03-eef5-4897-af52-804b279301eb" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
              <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_65b021e_1677491335912_422685_130052"/>
              <body> the words or set of words by which the ParametrizedDistribution is known. &lt;note&gt; This attribute supports multiple names in different contexts as well as multi-linguism.&lt;/note&gt;</body>
            </ownedComment>
            <name>ParameterizationName</name>
            <visibility>public</visibility>
            <type href="../../../DataTypes.xmi#STRING"/>
            <aggregation>composite</aggregation>
